> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > CodeRabbit round 2. The blind spot was the scheduling check
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > if (!hrtimer_active(&de->arm_timer))
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > sun55i_de_schedule_arm(de);
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > hrtimer_active() stays true while the timer callback is running, so a
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > commit racing with sun55i_de_arm_timer() sees the hrtimer as active
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > even though the callback already decided not to re-arm (do_arm cleared
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > arm_pending) and will return HRTIMER_NORESTART: a staged cursor/overlay
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > update sits in arm_pending forever without a timer and never reaches
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > the hardware.
